        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$, $0$",
          "worked": "As $x\\to\\infty$, both $\\sqrt{x}$ and $x^n$ grow without bound for $n>0$, so their reciprocals approach $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}&=0\\\\\\lim_{x\\to\\infty}\\frac{1}{x^n}&=0\\end{align*}$$",
